From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:14:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/22] H5: expose per-glyph font facts

A device that extracts text needs more than `as_unicode()`: the raw
character code and CID (to decide what to emit for an unmapped glyph),
the encoding's glyph name, whether the font is embedded or has a
`ToUnicode` map, the writing mode, the advance, and the font's vertical
extent (to build a glyph box for clipping tests). All of these were
private.

`Glyph`, `OutlineGlyph` and `Type3Glyph` gain `char_code()`, `cid()`,
`font_kind()` (new `FontKind` enum), `is_vertical()`, `glyph_name()`,
`has_to_unicode()`, `is_embedded()`, `character_collection()`,
`advance()` and `ascent_descent()`.

`advance()` is in thousandths of text space as the interpreter applies
it: `/Widths`, `/W`/`/DW` (vertical: `/W2`/`/DW2`), standard-font
metrics, and for Type3 fonts the width mapped through `/FontMatrix`.
`ascent_descent()` is in text space units and read once when the font
is loaded: the font descriptor's `/Ascent` and `/Descent`; for Type3
fonts the `/FontBBox` mapped through `/FontMatrix`; for non-embedded
standard fonts without descriptor metrics the Adobe Core 14 AFM
`Ascender`/`Descender`. A pair whose ascent is not above its descent
(producers write `0 0` when they do not know) is reported as `None`.
A substituted UCS2 `CMap` does not count as a `ToUnicode` map, and
Type3 glyphs count as embedded.
